>In article <5JUN199413482012@author.gsfc.nasa.gov> buckleyj@author.gsfc.nasa.gov (JOE BUCKLEY) writes:
>>A simple question from a Nethack newbie.

>>What is the Pw attribute in the status line? I haven't been able
>>to find the info in the FAQ. Oh, yeah. And for the strength

>>attribute, I've noticed the second number, after a / when the
>>characters strength is 18. Please explain! Thankx!
>>
>This is from the game Dungeons and Dragons. Where all the attributes are
>between 3 and 18 (3 rolls of a 6 sided dice). The strength was then further
>extended to include percentile. Basicly, it means, the higher the number the
>better, a 18/** means 18/100% BTW.

I'd always found that a little confusing.  Someone once posted that
this implied a strength somewhere between 18 and 19.  Perhaps the
display should then show 18.XX instead of 18/XX.  When it gets
to 18/** it could show 19.  (I imagine there is some subtle 
difference between 18/50 and 18.5, but 18.5 might be easier to
understand even if it is a little inaccurate).
